---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout
  title="GxP Clinical Data Migration | KSM Technology Partners"
  description="Purpose-built clinical data migration for regulated pharma environments. Audit-ready lineage, access controls, and tooling built for GxP from the ground up."
>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 1: Hero
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Moving content is the easy part.</h1>
    <p>
      In a GxP environment, regulatory requirements run through every decision —
      every transfer, every access control choice, every deviation from the plan.
      Most teams don't underestimate the technical complexity. They underestimate
      what GxP adds to it.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="../contact" class="btn">Schedule a Scoping Workshop</a>
    </div>
    <p class="trust-line">Delivered at multiple top-10 pharma companies.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 2: Where GxP Complexity Lives
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Where GxP complexity lives in data migration</h2>
      <div class="grid-2 mt-2">

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <!-- TODO: Replace with document/mapping icon -->
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/><polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Data Mapping</h3>
          <p>Legacy-to-target translation must be solved before you move a single byte — for code, data, and structure.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <!-- TODO: Replace with shield/audit icon -->
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Auditability</h3>
          <p>Can you prove things changed only when and how you said? Transparency is required from start to finish.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <!-- TODO: Replace with lock icon -->
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Access Control</h3>
          <p>Not a post-migration task. Unauthorized access to study data is a regulatory event.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <!-- TODO: Replace with checklist icon -->
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="9 11 12 14 22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Documentation</h3>
          <p>A plan before, a report after, and a deviation record. Every pharma defines their own requirements — does your migration process support them?</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 3: Credibility
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="credibility-layout">
      <img
        src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/services/cdc_scientist.jpg`}
        alt="Scientist working in a regulated laboratory environment"
        class="credibility-image"
      />
      <div>
        <blockquote class="pullquote">
          <p>"We've run this at multiple top-10 pharma companies."</p>
          <footer>Data migration in regulated life sciences is a deep practice — not a side capability.</footer>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="prose">
          <blockquote>
            "The technical challenges are solvable. Derailments are almost always in planning, mapping, and governance — not execution."
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 4: Our Approach — Controlled, Not Big Bang
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Controlled. Not big bang.</h2>
      <p class="intro-para">
        We break the migration into executable, governable units — study-level
        groupings with discrete ownership, independent state, and safe retry.
        Active studies don't get disrupted. Cutover happens in managed waves.
      </p>
      <div class="grid-2 feature-grid">

        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Migration Units</h3>
          <p>Study-level or equivalent groupings with clear ownership and status.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Per-Unit State</h3>
          <p>Each unit tracks its own state independently — safely retryable without affecting completed work.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Controlled Cutover</h3>
          <p>Managed transitions in waves, not a single high-risk switchover.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Bounded Scope</h3>
          <p>Clearly defined operational limits at every stage.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 5: Purpose-Built Tooling (KMT)
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="tooling-layout">

      <div>
        <h2>Purpose-built tooling for regulated data migration into Domino.</h2>
        <p class="intro-para">
          The KSM Migration Toolkit (KMT) was built specifically for the challenges
          of migrating clinical data into modern platforms like Domino.
          This is not a generic ETL tool adapted for this use case. It was designed for it.
        </p>

        <div class="capability-list">

          <div class="capability-item">
            <h3>Infrastructure-as-code execution</h3>
            <p>Via Terraform — deterministic, repeatable, peer-reviewed before it touches target systems.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="capability-item">
            <h3>Native Domino connector</h3>
            <p>Provisions organizations, projects, volumes, access controls, and syncpoints as code.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="capability-item">
            <h3>Git-managed configuration</h3>
            <p>Every change is traceable, reviewable, and auditable.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="image-placeholder">
        <img
          src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/services/saga_screenshot_graph.png`}
          alt="Lineage graph showing jobs, datasets, and transfers connected in a navigable audit graph"
          style="border-radius: var(--radius);"
        />
        <figcaption class="image-caption">Every job. Every dataset. Every transfer. Connected in a navigable, auditable graph — built during the migration, not reconstructed afterward.</figcaption>
      </figure>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 6: Audit Trail
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Your auditor gets evidence, not assurances.</h2>
      <p class="intro-para">Documentation as a byproduct of execution — not assembled after the fact.</p>

      <div class="grid-2 audit-grid">

        <div class="audit-item">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Timestamped Events</h3>
            <p>Every step emits a lineage event with a unique run ID — source to staging, staging to target.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="audit-item">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Auto-attached Results</h3>
            <p>Validation results, checksums, and row counts automatically attached to the lineage record.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="audit-item">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="9 11 12 14 22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Built During Execution</h3>
            <p>A complete audit trail — not reconstructed from logs.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="audit-item">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Deviation Records</h3>
            <p>When expected outcomes aren't met, it's captured and traceable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 7: How an Engagement Unfolds
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section" id="engagement">
    <h2>How an engagement unfolds.</h2>

    <ol class="timeline">

      <li class="phase">
        <div class="phase-number" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
        <div class="phase-content">
          <h3>Scoping Workshop</h3>
          <p>Data volumes, study types, source systems, regulatory constraints.</p>
          <p class="phase-output"><strong>Output:</strong> a clear picture of what you're migrating, and when.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="phase">
        <div class="phase-number" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
        <div class="phase-content">
          <h3>Mapping Exercise</h3>
          <p>Translate legacy model to target structure.</p>
          <p class="phase-output"><strong>Output:</strong> validated mapping spec and migration unit definitions.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="phase">
        <div class="phase-number" aria-hidden="true">3</div>
        <div class="phase-content">
          <h3>Pilot Migration</h3>
          <p>Execute first wave end-to-end. Produce first real validation package. Resolve edge cases.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="phase">
        <div class="phase-number" aria-hidden="true">4</div>
        <div class="phase-content">
          <h3>Migration at Scale</h3>
          <p>Controlled waves with cutover management, lineage visibility, and audit-ready documentation throughout.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 8: CTA (Bottom)
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="cta-banner">
    <h2>Every successful migration starts with understanding what you're migrating.</h2>
    <p>
      The Scoping Workshop is a structured, low-commitment first step. We assess
      your data volumes, study types, source system landscape, and regulatory
      constraints — and you leave with a migration you can execute with confidence.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="../contact" class="btn btn-outline">Schedule a Scoping Workshop</a>
      <a href="#engagement" class="cta-secondary-link">See how an engagement unfolds &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</PageLayout>

<style>
  /* Trust line in hero */
  .trust-line {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-mid);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Intro paragraphs */
  .intro-para {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  /* Credibility section layout */
  .credibility-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .credibility-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr;
    }
  }

  .credibility-image {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 280px;
    height: 360px;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 70% center;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    justify-self: center;
  }

  /* Pull quote (credibility section) */
  .pullquote {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .pullquote p {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .pullquote footer {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  /* Feature items (approach section) */
  .feature-grid {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .feature-item {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-white);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  .feature-item h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .feature-item p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Tooling two-column layout */
  .tooling-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .tooling-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* Capability list (tooling section) */
  .capability-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .capability-item {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-pale);
  }

  .capability-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .capability-item h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .capability-item p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Audit trail items */
  .audit-grid {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .audit-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .audit-item .card-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    margin-top: 0.1rem;
  }

  .audit-item h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .audit-item p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Engagement timeline */
  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }

  .phase {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    position: relative;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .phase:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .phase:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 19px;
    top: 40px;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--color-mid);
  }

  .phase-number {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-white);
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .phase-content {
    padding-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .phase-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .phase-content p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .phase-output {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* CTA secondary link */
  .cta-secondary-link {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: underline;
    align-self: center;
  }

  .cta-secondary-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-white);
  }
</style>
